  "id": "bipedal-locomotion",
  "term": "bipedal locomotion",
  "definition": "Bipedal locomotion is walking on two legs. In the context of gait adaptation, it involves adjusting movement to stay stable as conditions such as uphill or downhill walking change, using body-based and visual cues to help regulate walking speed.",
